  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Magnesium levulinate and Apolipoprotein E, mediated through Selgantolimod. Multiple paths indicate that Magnesium levulinate targets three different entities—Keratin, type II cytoskeletal 6A, Nucleoside diphosphate kinase A, and Plasma kallikrein—each of which is a target of Selgantolimod. Selgantolimod, in turn, is linked to Apolipoprotein E, suggesting a possible indirect pathway through which Magnesium levulinate may influence Apolipoprotein E. The scores across all three paths are consistent, indicating a moderate level of confidence in this relationship. However, the evidence is indirect and relies on the presence of a common intermediary (Selgantolimod), which may not be fully understood. The mechanisms by which Magnesium levulinate affects these targets remain unclear, and further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the proposed relationship.",
